[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
[color=#d4d4d8]Pins the world onto your map as you explore it, labelled, so you can find your way back to things without writing them down. Walk near an ore deposit, a crypt entrance, a wild beehive, an abandoned chest - it lands on your map with a name on it. The pins are saved to your character like hand-placed ones, and they stay put after you clear the node, so you can tick them off yourself when you're done.[/color]
[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[color=#d4d4d8]Use a mod manager (Vortex, r2modman, Thunderstore, or Gale) - it pulls in BepInEx for you. Manually: drop CarturMapPins.dll into BepInEx/plugins.[/color]
[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[color=#d4d4d8]What gets pinned: ore deposits, dungeon and cave entrances, goblin and draugr camps, wild beehives, runestones, abandoned chests, spawners, leviathans, traders, wisp fountains, high-value pickables (surtling cores, Yggdrasil shoots, eggs), and boss altars. Every category is a switch - turn off what you don't care about. Berries, mushrooms, crops and surface flint are off by default, since they'd carpet the map and bloat your save.
Emptied chests change icon: loot a chest and its pin switches to a looted marker, so cleared ones are obvious at a glance. Refill it and it switches back.
83 icons to pick from, one per category, so you can set ore, dungeons, chests and the rest to whatever reads best for you. Vanilla pin types still work if you'd rather stay with them.
Nothing is hardcoded to a prefab name - the list of what counts as ore, a beehive, or a pickable is built at runtime by looking at what components an object has, so it survives game updates and picks up modded content for free.
Commands: carturpins_clear removes every pin this mod placed (hand-placed pins are left alone), carturpins_count reports how many are on record.[/color]
[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[color=#d4d4d8]BepInEx pack for Valheim. Client-side only - the server doesn't need it and neither do the people you play with. Pairs well with Cartur's Compass and Clock, which puts these same pins on a compass bar.[/color]
